    <h1 class="about-article-title">Lance Andrei Espina</h1>
    <div class="dev-hero-role">Full Stack .NET Developer</div>
    <p class="about-article-lede">
        ECA-InFORMS was designed and built by Lance Andrei Espina, a full-stack .NET developer with
        7+ years of experience. He most recently served as a Software Engineer / Backend Developer at
        <strong>Accenture</strong> on <strong><a href="https://www.iras.gov.sg/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRAS</a> (Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore)</strong>, and is currently working
        full-time as an <strong>independent freelance developer and NCSC Project Development Officer III</strong>.
    </p>

    <section class="about-section">
        <h2 class="about-section-title">Background</h2>
        <p class="about-section-body">
            From October 2024, Lance worked as a Software Engineer / Backend Developer at Accenture,
            delivering backend services for <a href="https://www.iras.gov.sg/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRAS</a>
            (the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore) — using Azure, Docker, Kafka,
            Azure Repositories, C#.NET, Angular, and MSSQL, while adhering to SOLID principles and
            writing comprehensive unit tests before every deployment. Since then, he has continued as
            an independent freelance full-stack developer and NCSC Project Development Officer III,
            building end-to-end systems with Blazor WebAssembly, ASP.NET Core, and Clean Architecture — to date.
        </p>
        <p class="about-section-body" style="margin-top:12px;">
            Earlier in his career, Lance built government information systems for the Department of
            Social Welfare and Development in the Caraga Region — including a Social Pension
            Information System processing over 300,000 records and 6 million+ payrolls — plus systems
            for local government units, shipping companies, and hospitality businesses.
        </p>
    </section>

